  "prediction_basis": "Frozen 2026-10-08 before any qualified run, from reading DANDELION 0.1.0 R/DANDELION.R and qvalue 2.44.0 (Bioconductor; R/qvalue.R, R/pi0est.R at ce7605b2) in full, and checked in the sandbox (R 4.3.3; DANDELION from the CRAN 0.1.0 source; qvalue built from the ce7605b2 mirror commit -- NOT the qualified artifacts). Native-route condition: n >= 10, >= 4 distinct post-clamp values AND max >= 0.95, because pi0est's default smoother (lambda = 0.05..0.95) tabulates findInterval(p, lambda) and a missing top bin enters smooth.spline as NA, which stops ('missing or infinite values in inputs are not allowed'); safe_qvalues turns that error into BH. The warning route is NOT constructed: qvalue 2.44.0's own R code has no warning() call, so only R internals could raise one; that branch is covered by the test double (tests/unit/test_inference_backend_trace.py). EXPOSURE OUTCOMES (ruling 2026-10-08g): run_dandelion_for_exposure returns NULL at four guards (no trans genes; fewer than 2 valid genes; a NA or negative pi0 estimate; a non-positive mixture weight sum) -- the first two follow from the inputs (structural, predicted by pair_plan); the last two are mixture-estimation failures of an ELIGIBLE exposure. Every trans p-value equal to 1 drives nonnullPropEst's trans-side estimate negative (pi0a = -0x1.e7bab1690b2p-7 measured in the sandbox for 30 and 31 genes) while the burden side stays valid; an exposure absent from the filtered annotation never reaches run_dandelion_for_exposure (measured in the sandbox). Both were checked in the sandbox with the actual-call exposure recorder before this specification was frozen.",
